WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 5: On the Farm.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.403
In this unit you will learn about the farm.

3
00:00:06.483 --> 00:00:13.742
You will name the farm animals and the sounds they
make, learn farm words like tractor, barn and field,

4
00:00:13.822 --> 00:00:19.157
and talk about the work people do on
a farm — feeding, planting and picking.

5
00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:24.999
You will see how animals and plants grow:
a chick from an egg, a bean from a seed.

6
00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:29.274
You will hear a gentle story about helping and working hard.

7
00:00:29.354 --> 00:00:35.401
Say the words out loud — this is about
speaking with confidence, not perfect spelling.

8
00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:41.386
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:49.371
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
farm animals (cow, hen, chick, duck, sheep, goat, horse…)

10
00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:54.344
You will also say the sound each
animal makes (moo, cluck, quack, baa…)

11
00:00:54.424 --> 00:01:00.088
You will also name farm places and things
(farm, barn, field, tractor, egg, seed).

12
00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:02.679
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:02.759 --> 00:01:08.440
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: cow, hen, chick, duck, goose, pig.

14
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.633
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

15
00:01:14.713 --> 00:01:20.513
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Little Hen and Talk about On the Farm.

16
00:01:20.593 --> 00:01:25.594
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

17
00:01:25.674 --> 00:01:29.949
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

18
00:01:30.029 --> 00:01:33.392
The first language focus is Name a farm animal.

19
00:01:33.472 --> 00:01:34.930
Name one farm animal.

20
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:40.131
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a cow, an ox.

21
00:01:40.211 --> 00:01:44.892
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:44.972 --> 00:01:49.171
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:49.251 --> 00:01:52.679
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:59.835
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:01:59.915 --> 00:02:01.483
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:01.563 --> 00:02:08.432
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:02:08.512 --> 00:02:15.525
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
